			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of <i>any
				devouring monster,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				35
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				39
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				841
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>moth,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				760
			</span></i> (Rhodian in this sense acc. to Sch.).—In late
			codd. (as those of <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
			</span></i>) freq. written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φάλαινα;</span> but
			cod.Rav. of <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
			</span></i>, and the best codd. of <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Babr.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
			</span></i>, and <i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
			</span></i> (the Pap. of <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Dict.</u>
			</span></i> is indistinct) have <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φάλλ-;</span>
			cf. sq.; the metre requires a long first syll. in <i><span class="en">
				Babr.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nonn.
			</span></i>, and admits it elsewhere; in Lat. the best spelling is
				<i>ballaena.</i></div>
